A||||13||SloPonti||Rebuilding a high performace 2.5 L-help
Z||000000||SloPonti||08-31-99||08:36 PM||||i a rebuilding a 2.5l and i have heard of a making a 205 horsepower out of this little 4 banger-does anyone know about this?  and were do i look for parts for this motor!<br>thanks
Z||000001||88 Fiero||08-31-99||08:44 PM||||Slo...back in the 80's you can rebuild that 2.5 liter with the use of the SD4 package. A guy in the east coast got hold one of this package. his car is a stock '84 2.5 liter. He punched it to 2.7 liter with an output of 275 hp. The SD4 is the engine used in the IMSA and GTU racing...
Z||000002||batboy||08-31-99||09:01 PM||||I personally don't think the 2.5 will hold up very long if modified that much, but here's a URL for you to check out:<p>http://www.amotion.com/p4.html
Z||000003||batboy||08-31-99||09:03 PM||||The Super Duty 2.5 is a different story. They are a racing engine and hold up extemely well to high performance.
Z||000004||SloPonti||08-31-99||10:09 PM||||that is what i want info on is the 2.5 liter superduty or anything that will help me gain horsepower and were to get the parts!<br>thanks guys
Z||000005||88 Fiero||08-31-99||10:18 PM||||Well...the company that did the SD4 engine for the 4 cylinder is Callies performance Products. Here is the phone no. but I don't know if it's current...419-435-2711. They are  located in Fostoria, Ohio...Good luck...
Z||000006||batboy||09-01-99||02:34 AM||||Building a super duty engine cost several thousands of dollars. Here are a couple URLs for the 2.5 SD engine:<p>http://www.jps.net/gtracer/sd4/SuperDuty4.htm<p>http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/
Z||000007||DJRice||09-01-99||07:33 AM||||For the several thousand dollars it would take to hype up the 2.5L, I thinking one should just add the 4 extra cylinders, if you  know what I mean.....
Z||000008||batboy||09-01-99||04:03 PM||||Or at least 2 more cylinders. There are some really fast V6's out there.
Z||000009||SloPonti||09-01-99||04:13 PM||||well i don't have several thousands of dollars so how could i hop up my 4 banger?<br>i have a extra 2.5 and i am going to start to rebuild it-any tips on how to make it better would help out!<br>thanks
Z||000010||batboy||09-01-99||06:29 PM||||Put in a higher lift cam, install a good header/exhaust system, and beef up the ignition system. Anything more than that will began making the engine unreliable. The iron duke can't take much more than 125 hp and live a long life.
Z||000011||theogre||09-01-99||06:45 PM||||you can convert to a v6 cheaper than you might think. Try Kick Hill Farm. They have the whole package ready to stuff in.<p> <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com</A> 
Z||000012||lowCG||09-01-99||08:50 PM||||There are a lot of performance products/technology left over from the sixties,when that engine was used x2 in several Pontiac models in drag racing,with success too.<br>I would start with an HEI distributor,equal length header(if you can find one,otherwise use the stock,fabricated manifold),a set of Weber 45DCOE carburetors/manifold,and a 290 degree cam(solid lifter),full dynamic balance.That should put you right around 200HP,with anything over 9:1 compression.Stock rods should be more than adequate for that kind of use.
Z||000013||Phantom Rage||09-01-99||09:05 PM||||Hey Orge, that's one sweet site.  Thx <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
